WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.509
- Is it true that you gave Marvel feedback

00:00:02.509 --> 00:00:04.608
on all the Marvel movies?

00:00:04.608 --> 00:00:05.670
- I gotta be honest,

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.376
everything that happened
in my first year at Marvel

00:00:07.376 --> 00:00:09.360
was such a blur.
- But did you?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.130
- But I probably did.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.240
Every time I see a new movie,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.527
I'm texting Kevin or Victoria,

00:00:13.527 --> 00:00:17.669
like, "Hey, so next time
maybe try this instead,

00:00:17.669 --> 00:00:19.707
but like you're on the right track."

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:21.810
- Oh my God.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.100
- They can't say no to me now.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.020
- Should you be in school?
- No,

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.720
I got cast on the last day of high school.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.770
- Wow.
- What is your life?

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.090
- Perfect graduation present

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.326
considering I didn't get
one 'cause of COVID, so.

00:00:32.326 --> 00:00:33.360
- Yeah, well, there,

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.320
you did though.
- Oh

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.430
We don't feel real bad.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.263
- Yeah.

00:00:36.263 --> 00:00:38.040
No one feels bad for you right now.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.020
So wait, one of the
coolest things though is

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.300
you are Marvel's first Muslim superhero.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.338
That's like really cool too.

00:00:43.338 --> 00:00:45.297
Does that,
(audience applauding)

00:00:45.297 --> 00:00:46.130
so cool.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:46.963
Does it feel,

00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:48.837
cause the inclusivity is awesome.

00:00:48.837 --> 00:00:50.779
Does you feel pressure 'cause of that

00:00:50.779 --> 00:00:52.107
'cause you're holding something down

00:00:52.107 --> 00:00:53.475
all by yourself right now?

00:00:53.475 --> 00:00:55.083
- Nope.
- Nope.

00:00:56.077 --> 00:00:57.177
- I love you.

00:00:57.177 --> 00:00:58.290
- No, I mean like,
- You know, what's great?

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.940
A Catholic, a Muslim, and a Jew.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.197
We should go walk into a bar.

00:01:01.197 --> 00:01:02.822
- I'm not Catholic.
- Christian.

00:01:02.822 --> 00:01:05.100
- I'm
- Let's walk into a bar.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.664
I know something really
funny might happen.

00:01:06.664 --> 00:01:07.753
- There's this really great joke.

00:01:07.753 --> 00:01:09.420
- I love it.
- It's coming.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.820
No, but there's a lot of pressure

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.050
with being the first of anything.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.580
I just, I don't think about it.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.842
I can't wake up every morning and be like,

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.450
"You're the first Muslim
Pakistani superhero.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.283
Do good, okay?

00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:20.460
For your people."

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.120
But like, no, it's just, the
superhero part is so cool.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.223
And it's just like working with my idols.

00:01:27.631 --> 00:01:29.310
There's so much inspiration

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:32.069
and representation for
me behind the camera.

00:01:32.069 --> 00:01:33.630
- Yeah.
- All the creatives

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:36.480
on our show have such
an emotional attachment

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.830
to this character and to the story

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.293
and they're bringing so much of that

00:01:39.293 --> 00:01:41.880
and I think that's just why I'm here.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.370
- I think it's awesome that
you are so chill about it too

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.200
because I think that's also.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.353
I came in the industry at 19 as well

00:01:48.353 --> 00:01:50.460
and everybody would say,
"Oh, do you feel pressure?"

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.293
And it was so funny.

00:01:51.293 --> 00:01:52.560
I got that question, I was like, "No,

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.490
but should I?"
- Yeah.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:55.893
- I was like, I would freak out

00:01:55.893 --> 00:01:58.794
because I think people naturally
want to ask the question

00:01:58.794 --> 00:02:01.530
but sometimes I think
when you are 19 years old,

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.300
you're just like, "I'm just
like doing what I love.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.140
And it's like fun."

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.463
And there's no reason other than that

00:02:07.463 --> 00:02:09.030
which is kind of really beautiful.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.440
- Yeah. I'd do this for free.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.177
My dad was like, "Don't say that."

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.940
- I'm sure your agent said that too.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.870
- Her life is in insane.
- It's so weird,

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:19.950
so wonderful.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:20.946
- I know.
- It's amazing.

00:02:20.946 --> 00:02:22.653
You're like a dream come true, young lady.

00:02:22.653 --> 00:02:26.583
- [Kelly] You're a home
town girl who's killing it.

